# Stage 4c — isJuralOppositeOf on the Duty <-> Privilege axis.
#
# Second axis of Hohfeld's square. The correlative swaps the holder and keeps
# the content; the OPPOSITE keeps the holder and negates the content:
#   Duty(A->B, x)  is the opposite of  Privilege(A->B, ¬x)     [O(x) ≡ ¬P(¬x)]
#
# POSITIONS ARE DIRECTED, which is why the holder alone is not enough. An agent
# may have a duty to do x toward B and a privilege not to do it toward C, and
# that is not opposition: it is Hohfeld's multital analysis, two distinct
# jural relations. The same holder AND the same counterparty are therefore
# required.
#
# The counterparty is compared on the conferring NORMS, because the position's
# own counterparty (hasPositionCounterparty) is derived through a chain and is
# not materialised. An unannotated counterparty is treated as non-conflicting,
# as in stage 5: a declared reading, not a neutral one.
PREFIX norma: <https://w3id.org/def/norma-o#>
CONSTRUCT { ?duty norma:isJuralOppositeOf ?priv . }
WHERE {
  ?nd norma:confersLegalPosition ?duty .
  ?np norma:confersLegalPosition ?priv .
  ?duty a norma:Duty      ; norma:hasPositionHolder ?a ; norma:concernsLegalAction ?x .
  ?priv a norma:Privilege ; norma:hasPositionHolder ?a ; norma:concernsLegalAction ?y .
  ?x norma:isNegationOf ?y .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?nd norma:hasCounterparty ?b1 . ?np norma:hasCounterparty ?b2 . FILTER(?b1 != ?b2)
  }
  # INCOMPATIBLE conditions, the same filter as 05b and 05c. Two norms
  # activated by opposite branches of one condition never coincide in a case,
  # so their positions never coexist either and there is no opposition to
  # report. Without this the two routes to conflict disagreed: jural opposition
  # fired where deontic contradiction, correctly, did not.
  FILTER NOT EXISTS {
    ?c norma:hasTrigger ?g1, ?g2 .
    ?g1 norma:activatesNorm ?nd ; norma:hasOutcome ?o1 .
    ?g2 norma:activatesNorm ?np ; norma:hasOutcome ?o2 .
    FILTER(?o1 != ?o2)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?h1 norma:activatesNorm ?nd . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?c norma:hasTrigger ?h1 } }
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?h2 norma:activatesNorm ?np . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?c norma:hasTrigger ?h2 } }
  }
}
